findings.problem:
The template assumes that each register sheet carries the 94c049d design text and itemised entries. The register's sheets (register lines 1274-1566) carry only paragraph ids and section pointers. With the sheets as the only design input:
- no 94c049d sentence can be quoted, so every 'architectural weakness' or 'design trade-off' record fails validation check 3, or rests on a quote from memory;
- the WD rule's 'register sheet's 94c049d text' does not exist;
- the conformance checklist is a list of id ranges with no requirement text, so class (1) conformance cannot be assessed;
- 'every item of the sheets' (check 4) is not defined by the sheet structure;
- E6 and check 6 accept any 94c049d id 'present in the register sheet', but the sheets limit architectural grounds to the (C) ids and trade-off grounds to the (B) ids of each boundary.

result.summary:
I reviewed the implementation and held-constant side of the design-and-controls register, plus 23-am1-prompts.py and 23-am1-prompts-evaluated.md, against the code at 3320375 and the nine run traces. I found 1 major, 6 minor and 2 nit defects.

**What checked out:**
- **Prompts script.** I ran it unmodified through an importlib wrapper that changed only OUT, with output written to the scratch verify folder. The output is byte-identical to 23-am1-prompts-evaluated.md (both SHA-256 b02a7f70…). The script's own hash is c26e6170…, as the register states.
- **Static/dynamic split.** The split rule is sound. Every seam has 1 system and 1 user-template variant per arm and per run, with 0 unparsed messages.
- **Prompt hashes.** I re-derived every hash from the 3320375 constants with ast, and all match:
  - recorded prompts: gatekeeper, resolver, grounding, support check, and the scalar-replaced extraction template 725f1c00 (2,445 characters);
  - code-derived prompts: expansion generator f570f53a (1,412 characters), judge 8469921d (1,934), RAG a2d74d5e (1,390) and WD daf30b70 (3,516).
  - The extraction template without the scalar replacement would hash f7d42d84, so `expansion_force_scalar` was on.
- **As-run switch sets.** All nine coldstart.json `cycle2_flags` blocks match the register's switch sets:
  - A0: only the two instrument repairs on;
  - A1: all ten repairs on;
  - A2: ten repairs plus four contracts;
