findings.problem:
The failure-policy statement covers only LLM seams. Embedding errors are swallowed silently at five call sites, each falling back to a different deterministic path:
- the resolver shortlist sends the whole registry;
- value-matched retrieval falls back to stem containment;
- the relevance filter falls back to compact matching;
- canonicalisation does nothing;
- A2 equivalence treats the values as not equivalent.

No trace or coldstart field would show such a fallback. The run logs do settle it: there were no embedding failures. That check should be in H.

Separately, line 1745 is wrong for RAG. The RAG lane passed `--embedding-cache`, and its vectors are kept with their model id.

